# Frontend and config files of vLLM PR #64534 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64534) ("[Model] Add Mistral Large 4"), merged onto
# vLLM v0.30.0 (the releases/v0.30.0 image runs ced6857a = v0.30.0): for each file, `git merge-file` of
# v0.30.0 (ours), the PR parent 2d40c0609 (base) and the PR head bd4fa2633 (theirs), so the
# file is v0.30.0 plus exactly the PR's hunks. The conflicts were all at import lines that
# v0.30.0 spells differently (vllm.entrypoints.chat_utils, not vllm.renderers.chat_utils);
# they keep v0.30.0's imports and add the PR's (AnyResponseFormat, to_mistral_response_format).
# Two adaptations to v0.30.0: parser/mistral.py drops one PR line, a check_json_nesting()
# call (v0.30.0 has no such helper, and its parser had no nesting check either); and in
# configs/mistral.py the annotations of the PR's new get_mistral_large_4_dspark_config are
# spelled PretrainedConfig, as v0.30.0 imports it (the PR parent renamed it PreTrainedConfig).
# Gates: tests/build_gates.py (pr_files).
#
# Every file REPLACES a stock v0.30.0 file. One line per file:
#   <sha256 of vendor/<path>>  <path>  replaces <sha256 of the stock v0.30.0 file>
# patches/install_pr_files.py installs a file only over the recorded stock bytes (or over its own
# bytes, a re-run), and refuses anything else.
# PR head blob sha256 (theirs, for re-vendoring): configs/mistral.py 40a82fb3c72d,
# tokenizers/mistral.py 135d09e55878, renderers/mistral.py a345f9b40fa1,
# serve/tokenize/protocol.py 431e8dee56e8, parser/mistral.py c9c3c70abcad.
